cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenCaseLaw, please cite the software and the dataset."
title: "OpenCaseLaw: an open Swiss legal corpus and citation graph"
abstract: >-
  OpenCaseLaw is an open, multilingual corpus of Swiss court decisions with a
  resolved cross-court citation graph, federal and cantonal legislation, and
  interpretive links to legislative history, commentary, scholarship and
  federal administrative practice. It is served as live infrastructure over
  the Model Context Protocol and REST, and released as CC0 bulk data.
type: software
authors:
